#! mathcas 2 notebook

#% title
# z_transform

#% text
# `z_transform(f, n, z)` gives the Z transform `sum(f*z^-n, [n, 0, inf])` of the sequence `f`.

#% text
# `z_transform(f, [n, m], [z, w])` transforms in several variables.

#% section
# Details

#% item
# Sums term by term; terms with undefined functions stay as `z_transform` calls; shifts `f(n + k)` and `f(n - k)` of an undefined `f` give its transform and initial values.

#% item
# `a^n g(n)` gives `G(z/a)`, `n g(n)` gives `-z G'(z)`, `unit_step(n - k) g(n)` gives `z^-k` times the transform of `g(n + k)`, `discrete_delta(n - k)` gives `z^-k`.

#% item
# Trigonometric functions are written as exponentials; factorial powers and Pochhammer symbols of `n` as polynomials; other sequences go to `sum`.

#% item
# `generate_conditions: true` gives the region of convergence `abs(z) > r`.

#% section
# Examples

#% subsection
# Basic examples

#% cell
z_transform(a^n, n, z)
#% output
#= z/(z - a)

#% cell
z_transform(n^2, n, z)
#% output
#= z*(1 + z)/(-1 + z)^3

#% subsection
# Scope

#% cell
z_transform(n*(n + 1)*(-1/2)^n, n, z)
#% output
#= -8*z^2/(1 + 2*z)^3

#% cell
z_transform(sin(w*n), n, z)
#% output
#= z*sin(w)/(1 - 2*z*cos(w) + z^2)

#% cell
z_transform([discrete_delta(n), discrete_delta(n - 5)], n, z)
#% output
#= [1, z^-5]

#% cell
z_transform(unit_step(n - 3), n, z)
#% output
#= 1/(z^2*(-1 + z))

#% cell
z_transform(a^(n + m), [n, m], [z, w])
#% output
#= -w*z/((a - z)*(w - a))

#% text
# Undefined functions:

#% cell
z_transform(f(n + 1), n, z)
#% output
#= z*(-f(0) + z_transform(f(n), n, z))

#% cell
z_transform(a^n*f(n), n, z)
#% output
#= z_transform(f(n), n, z/a)

#% text
# Trigonometric sequences and sequences with factorials:

#% cell
z_transform(cos(w*n), n, z)
#% output
#= z*(z - cos(w))/(1 - 2*z*cos(w) + z^2)

#% cell
z_transform(1/factorial(n), n, z)
#% output
#= exp(z^-1)

#% cell
z_transform(2^n/factorial(n), n, z)
#% output
#= exp(2/z)

#% text
# Binomial coefficients and shifted reciprocals:

#% cell
z_transform(binomial(n, 2), n, z)
#% output
#= z/(-1 + z)^3

#% cell
z_transform(1/(n + 1), n, z)
#% output
#= -z*log(1 - z^-1)

#% text
# A step times a polynomial, and a sequence with no closed sum in `z`, given by a hypergeometric function:

#% cell
z_transform(unit_step(n)*(n + 1)^2, n, z)
#% output
#= (1 + z)*z^2/(-1 + z)^3

#% cell
z_transform(1/(n^2 + 1), n, z)
#% output
#= hypergeometric_pfq([-im, im, 1], [1 - im, 1 + im], z^-1)

#% text
# A delay of an undefined sequence brings in its values at negative `n`:

#% cell
z_transform(f(n - 2), n, z)
#% output
#= f(-2) + f(-1)/z + z_transform(f(n), n, z)/z^2

#% subsection
# Options

#% cell
z_transform(a^n, n, z, generate_conditions: true)
#% output
#= conditional_expression(z/(z - a), abs(z) > abs(a))

#% text
# The region of convergence of a sum of exponentials is that of the larger one:

#% cell
z_transform(2^n + 3^n, n, z, generate_conditions: true)
#% output
#= conditional_expression(z*((-3 + z)^-1 + (-2 + z)^-1), abs(z) > 3)

#% text
# A number for `z` gives the value of the sum there, exact, machine or at the precision of `z`:

#% cell
z_transform((1/2)^n, n, 3)
#% output
#= 6/5

#% cell
z_transform((1/2)^n, n, 3.0)
#% output
#= 1.2000000000000002

#% cell
z_transform((1/2)^n, n, n(3, 30))
#% output
#= 1.2000000000000000000000000000000000

#% subsection
# Properties and relations

#% cell
inverse_z_transform(z_transform(n*2^n, n, z), z, n)
#% output
#= n*2^n

#% text
# At a number the value is the sum:

#% cell
sum((1/2)^n*3^-n, [n, 0, inf])
#% output
#= 6/5

#% cell
z_transform(2^n, n, 3)
#% output
#= 3

#% subsection
# Possible issues

#% text
# A sequence that grows too fast has no transform; for a number `z` inside the region where the sum diverges the call stays (the closed form there is only the analytic continuation), and exactly on the boundary too:

#% cell
z_transform(2^n, n, 1.5)
#% output
#= z_transform(2^n, n, 1.5)

#% cell
z_transform(2^n, n, 2)
#% output
#= z_transform(2^n, n, 2)

#% text
# `factorial(n)` grows too fast for the sum to converge and stays a call; in a sum, the part with an undefined sequence stays a call and the rest is transformed:

#% cell
z_transform(factorial(n), n, 3.0)
#% output
#= z_transform(factorial(n), n, 3.0)

#% cell
z_transform(f(n) + 2*a^n, n, z)
#% output
#= 2*z/(z - a) + z_transform(f(n), n, z)

#% text
# Fibonacci numbers and harmonic numbers have closed transforms, checked here against the sum at `z = 3`:

#% cell
z_transform(fibonacci(n), n, 3.0) - 3.0/(9 - 3 - 1)
#% output
#= 0.0

#% cell
z_transform(harmonic_number(n), n, 3.0) - sum(harmonic_number(k)/3.0^k, [k, 0, 200])
#% output
#= 1.1102230246251565e-16

#% text
# `working_precision:` is not an option; the call is returned with it:

#% cell
z_transform(a^n, n, z, working_precision: 30)
#% output
#= z_transform(a^n, n, z, working_precision: 30)

#% section
# See also

#% text
# `inverse_z_transform`, `sum`, `discrete_delta`, `laplace_transform`
